    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25481" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăbĕrĭus</span></b> ,
		a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a Roman</i> gens; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">so esp. D. Laberius,</span>”
				<i>a knight, celebrated as a composer of mimes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 7, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">12, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				10, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 39</span></i>; Sen. de Ira, 2, 11;
					<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2,
			7</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lă-bĕrĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to</i> D. Laberius, <i>Laberian</i>: versus, Sen. de Ira, 2, 11, 4.</div>
